    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "13. Terrain",
    "ruleNumber": "13.08",
    "order": 176,
    "anchor": "13.08",
    "summary": "For a ranged attack, check every model in the target unit. A model qualifies if:\n\n- it has **INFANTRY**, **BEASTS** or **SWARM** while within a **terrain area**, or\n- a **terrain feature** or [Obscuring](vsdata:core-rule/obscuring) terrain prevents the attacking model from seeing it in full\n\nWhen all the target's models qualify, it has **Benefit of Cover**: worsen the attack's **BS** by 1.\n\n**[[IGNORES COVER]](vsdata:weapon-ability/ignores-cover)** bypasses it. **[Stealth](vsdata:core-ability/stealth)**, **[Indirect Shooting](vsdata:core-rule/indirect-shooting)** and **[Smokescreen](vsdata:ability/core.smokescreen)** have their own ways to grant it. Under **[Hit Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls)**, an unmodified 6 is a **critical hit** before comparing the roll with **BS**.",
